  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "All seven completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, leaving the RNA representation choice as the largest unexplored design dimension. The current best config (config_019: scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile, acc=0.542) establishes a strong baseline. config_007 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is an exact A/B comparison that changes only the RNA encoder from scgpt to pca_n2000, isolating the effect of learned vs. linear RNA representations. If PCA performs comparably, it indicates the task does not require a complex RNA encoder and simplifies the design space; if it underperforms significantly, it confirms that a learned representation is essential and motivates further comparison with scvi_n200. This single-variable experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about one of the most impactful design choices while keeping all other settings at their empirically best values (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, imagenet_vit_l), making it the highest-information next step under a limited budget."
}

